```plaintext
0result.sql
```

0result.sql is preferred because:

• It uses EXTRACT(YEAR FROM n.Year)=2018, which is clearer and still hits the single 2018 row, whereas 2result.sql hard‑codes the full date string.  
• It employs SAFE_DIVIDE to guard against potential division‑by‑zero in the commuting‑percentage test; 2result.sql does not, and would error if a county had employed_pop = 0.  
The rest of the logic (Wisconsin filter, >5 % commuting threshold, selection of average prenatal weeks) is identical, so 0result.sql is the safer, more robust choice.